# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Connor Edwards et al. (2026). Benchmarking Universal Machine-Learned Interatomic Potentials for High-Temperature Metal-Organic Framework Chemistry.
#   arXiv (Cornell University). doi:10.48550/arxiv.2604.25262  arXiv:2604.25262v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2604.25262v1 (sha256 d1b5bddb41bedfb5...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 272 (Dataset/benchmark). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/edwards2026benchmarking.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the new 40 ps PBE-D3 AIMD data set of nine Zn and Zr
# MOFs at 300, 1000 and 2000 K, and the energy, force and stress MAEs of
# the universal models ORB-v3, MACE-MP-0a and MACE-MPA-0 on it (Table 1,
# averaged over MOFs and temperatures; 300 K values of ORB-v3 from the
# Conclusion). The two fairchem models are not encoded (architecture not
# named). Per-temperature and per-MOF errors (Fig. 3) and the ORB-v3 ramp
# MD losses (Fig. 4) are figure-only.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
