###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# No timings are given. ORB-v3 ramp MD (1 ns, 300 to 2000 K) was run for
# all nine MOFs and 300 sampled structures per MOF were recomputed with DFT.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - The fairchem ODAC23 and OMAT models are named only by their training data (fairchem 2.13.0); their architecture is not stated, so they are not encoded as runs. Their Table 1 MAEs are 11.31 and 3.21 meV/atom, 188.30 and 94.01 meV/A, 401.66 and 293.98 MPa (300 K for OMAT: 0.67 meV/atom, 83.49 meV/A, 89.12 MPa).
# - The ORB-v3 and MACE-MP-0a checkpoints (size, conservative or direct) are not stated, so all models are paper-local runs. Stress MAEs in MPa are converted to GPa. The weighted loss (energy:force:stress 1:100:1) of Table 1 is not encoded.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: datacite).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/edwards2026benchmarking.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

